WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.634 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Chuckling ]

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:04.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hi.
-I'm Ron.

00:00:04.404 --> 00:00:08.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's the only
living footage of Ron.

00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:12.278 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:14.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, you have to remember
that you get hired,

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:17.183 size:78% position:39%
and there's not a lot
of hand-holding here.

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:19.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I remember
having moments

00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:21.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
of, like,
"No one thinks I'm funny.

00:00:21.388 --> 00:00:22.622 size:88% position:44% line:92%
This is gonna be rough."

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:24.858 line:92%
I was always kind of awestruck

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:28.094 align:start size:94% position:6%
at how serious
the place can be at times.

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:31.231 size:81% position:41%
And I thought, "Wait.
This is a comedy show.

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:32.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
We should be
[bleep] [bleep] up."

00:00:32.599 --> 00:00:36.636 size:88% position:44%
And so I would sometimes
sit in this writers room

00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:39.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
as Chip Kudrow,
Lisa Kudrow's brother.

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:41.174
Or maybe I'd just put on glasses
or something.

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:43.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
Steve Higgins would be like,
"Can I help you?"

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:45.111 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like,
"Yeah, I'm Chip Kudrow."

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:47.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughing ]
"Lisa Kudrow's brother."

00:00:47.414 --> 00:00:48.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh."
"Yeah, I'm guest-writing.

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:50.283 align:start size:94% position:6%
Lorne didn't tell you?
Anyway..."

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:51.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
They would
actually go through

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:53.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
the normal constructive proces
of giving notes,

00:00:53.787 --> 00:00:55.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then Steve would go,
"Chip, any ideas?"

00:00:55.822 --> 00:00:58.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'd just be like,
"This one's good to go."

00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:01.528
We did a lot of stuff waitin
for Lorne at the read-through.

00:01:01.528 --> 00:01:05.165
One time, I organized that w
all, like, when Lorne walks in

00:01:05.165 --> 00:01:06.499 size:75% position:38% line:92%
just go, "Surprise!"

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:09.869 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, of course,
Lorne was like, "Are we done

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:12.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
Okay. Open on..."
[ Laughs ]

00:01:12.539 --> 00:01:13.440 size:78% position:39% line:92%
There was a sketch --

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:16.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were doing, like, a
"Smokey and the Bandit" parody

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:19.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I'm in these Wrangler jeans
a Western shirt,

00:01:19.646 --> 00:01:23.716 align:start size:94% position:6%
one of those sleeveless fleece
jackets, and a trucker hat

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:25.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
For some reason, we had
to tape it throughout the day,

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:27.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I just stayed in my costume
the whole day.

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:30.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I wore the costum
the next day.

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:32.525
There's this writer, Tom Gianas,
who's like,

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:36.429
"Please wear the costume
for the rest of the year."

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:37.697 line:92%
And that was like November

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:40.200
So I wore it every day
for the rest of the year.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:43.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think sometime in the spring
Alec Baldwin was hosting.

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:44.938 line:92%
And he came up to me, he's like,

00:01:44.938 --> 00:01:46.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Is that how you
normally dress?"

00:01:46.506 --> 00:01:48.308 line:92%
I go, "Oh, no, this is a bit

00:01:48.308 --> 00:01:49.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is a yearlong bit
I'm doing."

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:52.679 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Okay, good, because
it's not a good look for you."

00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:54.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Okay. Thank you
for telling me, Alec."

00:01:54.581 --> 00:01:57.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then there was this characte
Ron that I came up with

00:01:57.417 --> 00:01:58.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
with a fake mustache
and an ascot

00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:02.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
and this weird outfit
that I found at a thrift store

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:06.659 line:92%
[ Indistinct conversations ]

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:07.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hi.
-I'm Ron.

00:02:07.494 --> 00:02:10.196
-I never broke character.
I just went, "I'm Ron."

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:11.764 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Chuckles ]
-Yeah, this is Paula Pell.

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:13.800 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What do you do
here on the show, Ron?

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.802 line:92%
-I'm working for Jim Signorelli.

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:17.604 line:92%
-Oh, I forgot. I worked for Jim.

00:02:17.604 --> 00:02:19.939 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I'm his nanny.

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:22.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I also work
second camera unit.

00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:24.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And, yeah, I just started
showing up as Ron,

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:26.279 size:88% position:44% line:92%
who was really annoying.

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:28.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Ron, what are you doing?
-Having a snack.

00:02:28.715 --> 00:02:33.253
-There was one moment wher
we were in this writers room

00:02:33.253 --> 00:02:34.888 line:92%
watching Puff Daddy rehearse

00:02:34.888 --> 00:02:37.824 align:start size:94% position:6%
and someone said,
"Ron should go up onstage.

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:39.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
And before everyone
turned to see,

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:41.427 line:92%
I had sprinted out the door.

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:43.763 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's supposed to be
a closed set.

00:02:43.763 --> 00:02:45.431 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:48.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, this is when Ron
is just appearing

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.904 line:92%
on the stage with Puff Daddy

00:02:50.904 --> 00:02:53.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
I didn't really know what to d
once I got up there.

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:56.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, then I -- then we
shook hands. That was good

00:02:56.476 --> 00:02:58.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, Ron? What'd you thin
about Puff?

00:02:58.945 --> 00:03:01.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm not familiar --
He seemed fine.

00:03:01.548 --> 00:03:04.551 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.551 --> 00:03:04.951 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh.

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:08.388
If you go back and look
at the good-nights of that show,

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:10.790 line:92%
Ron might be in the good-nights.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:11.691 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I just have a feeling.

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:17.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Puff Daddy, John Goodman,
Paula Abdul, my man, Nick Lea.

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:18.031 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Happy Mother's Day!

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:19.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because of the nature
of the show,

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:21.901
the kind of day-to-day pressures
of having to produce materia

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:25.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
and things like that, so I was
always trying to find ways

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:27.340 line:92%
to make everyone remember

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:28.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we were all
on "Saturday Night Live."

00:03:28.808 --> 00:03:32.845
You know, this is supposed to be
a really fun job.

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:35.615 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Chuckles ]

